{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition","id":987080,"title":"What's been left out of 2nd edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-13T20:33:19-07:00","id":987080,"title":"What's been left out of 2nd edition?","content":"As I'm reading the manuscript, it's hard to figure out what's not there. I'm glad Contracts of Mirrors was put in. Are we missing Contracts of Dreams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T20:54:02-07:00","id":987085,"title":"","content":"It's still there, for the most part. But I imagine some of the powers have been either folded over or removed altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T21:03:57-07:00","id":987087,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can map old contracts to new contracts 1:1 like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:12:55-07:00","id":987181,"title":"","content":"You soooorrt of can. &quot;Can I cover the narrative bases&quot; maps well enough.<br /> <br /> Contract of Dream is in 2e. Pathfinder is ported directly. Dreamsteps replaces Dream 5. Cobblethought is now a basic rule. Dream 3 is arguably a core rule for changelings, but there is nothing to replace the concept space of &quot;make super dream-only weapons and armor.&quot; Im not sure that space is a good idea anymore, however, given the emphasis on physically being in the dream. Dream 2 is of limited utility in 2e, given that Dreamsteps is a thing. The narrative part of using a picture to manipulate dreams from afar isnt covered but, again, goes against the themes of 2e dreamwalking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:41:32-07:00","id":987510,"title":"","content":"Left out of the game or the playtest documents?<br /> <br /> Out of the playtest document is direct stuff on the True Fae &amp; Loyalists from the antagonist chapter, Toronto Freeholds Court contracts, Miami Court, possibly something else.<br /> <br /> The the only thing I can think of being left out of the actually Core Book is Eldrich Entitlement full (but you really have the mechanics for it), an update for every entitlement ever (not a realistic expectation), and I think acouple of settings that didn't make.<br /> <br /> Its seriously amazing what was fit in. Fetch rules including echoes, around a hundred kiths, six seemings, four sample freeholds with three to possibly five courts a piece with mantle, merits, and contracts, 3 entitlements, advice on building courts/kiths/ entitlements, rules for traveling the hedge, including trods, icons, goblin fruits, dream bastions and dreams, hedgespinning, dream weaving, Hedge Warping, Onierons, including Cambions have half mortals, Hedge Beasts, Hollows, Tokens, Hedge Tokens, 4 types of pledges (Sealings, Bargains, Oaths, and Goblin Vows), Changeling merits, some mortal merits, Fae Touched Merits, The Changeling Template, Fae Touched Template, Huntsmen and Huntsmem creation rules, Hubtsmen powers, Character Creation rules, new clarity rules, Contracts, Goblin Contracts, and I'm betting David has a few surprises yet.<br /> <br /> So clearly David has some how acquired 5 dots of the space Arcana!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:10:07-07:00","id":987636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=987181#post987181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You soooorrt of can. &quot;Can I cover the narrative bases&quot; maps well enough.<br /> <br /> Contract of Dream is in 2e. Pathfinder is ported directly. Dreamsteps replaces Dream 5. Cobblethought is now a basic rule. Dream 3 is arguably a core rule for changelings, but there is nothing to replace the concept space of &quot;make super dream-only weapons and armor.&quot; Im not sure that space is a good idea anymore, however, given the emphasis on physically being in the dream. Dream 2 is of limited utility in 2e, given that Dreamsteps is a thing. The narrative part of using a picture to manipulate dreams from afar isnt covered but, again, goes against the themes of 2e dreamwalking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just read the part on dreams. I love the fact that Cobblethought is a basic rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T02:14:48-07:00","id":987681,"title":"","content":"A minor note: Do Huntmen have access to contracts? in the playtest there was no mention about that, and it feels strange the changelings would be allowed to keep such an powerful advantage over their nemesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:11:11-07:00","id":987730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=987681#post987681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A minor note: Do Huntmen have access to contracts? in the playtest there was no mention about that, and it feels strange the changelings would be allowed to keep such an powerful advantage over their nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div> At the moment, they do not. Specifically, Huntsmen have the mortal template, plus Yearning abilities and 25XP. I suspect this is in no small part to encourage the ST to have the Huntsmen serve as trickster antagonists and not obvious combat brutes. You don't need alot of combat ability when a simple touch can kill someone and take their place.<br /> <br /> The Huntsment disguise themselves as a cop and slip on a pair of cuffs to the changeling, who expects to just slip out of them. Then, to the Lost's horror, he finds he cannot excape the shackles, nor can he escape the giant police dog's gaze as the cop car drives off through a Hedge gate. Or perhaps the changeling is taken while asleep and unwary, exhausted from fleeing for the night in an unsecured location. Or is betrayed by a fellow Lost who bargained for a Token of Reprieve. Or was attacked by a living statue, akin to the Weeping Angels of Doctor Who. <br /> <br /> Giving Contracts, however, would encourage a &quot;charge forwards and confront in combat, drag the target to the ground, and have at thee!&quot; mindset. Match up against each other. I don't think that's the intent of the game, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:21:59-07:00","id":987814,"title":"","content":"Huntsmen also have Arcadian Weapons so they are no slouch in combat, but most prefer trickery for a more entraininv hunt and for yearning.<br /> <br /> Giving Huntsmen contracts would take way from Loyalists as a threat.<br /> <br /> You could give Huntsmen Hedge Beast Companion at \u2022\u2022\u2022 as well.<br /> <br /> Each possible Antagonist has their niche, Fetches Echoes, Loyalists Changeling powers, Huntmens Yearning, Icons, and Arcadian Weapons, True Fae massive power, Cambions Glamour feeding, Incubi Dreamwalking, Succubi Dream Feeding, Hedge Beasts raw animalistic physical threats, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-15-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T02:07:16-07:00","id":989258,"title":"","content":"What is either missing or needs to be addressed in another book is the Grimm seeming, or rather their contract bonuses. So far I have not seen one, which makes character creation for them impossible without a good deal of houseruling, and normal contract gaining likewise less rewarding since you need to pay another experience to gain a contract bonus instead of having the opportunity for a free one. I do appreciate there is a word limit in an already cramped book, but it is frustrating having a seeming that is complete and yet feels like it is even more a work in progress due to it having no support in the actual work in progress core book.<br /> <br /> Do note, I love what is revealed already. i am just impatient and wanting more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:18:36-07:00","id":990729,"title":"","content":"Mobile Hollow is the only thing that I noticed not being present, and that only bothers me because I'm an RV nut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T20:02:38-07:00","id":990767,"title":"","content":"In the book but not previewed yet are the Miami and Paris Freeholds, and possibly one more if I'm remembering right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T23:14:32-07:00","id":990819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=990729#post990729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mobile Hollow is the only thing that I noticed not being present, and that only bothers me because I'm an RV nut.</div> </div> </div> </div> With the right contract you could take an animated RV as a retainer. Not a hollow, but you take it into the Hedge or into Ironside. Not sure if it needs gas anymore if you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:53:25-07:00","id":992428,"title":"","content":"&quot;Chapter One: What Comes Before Here, we talk the fundamental aspects of what makes a changeling. We discuss kiths, which are the mutated forms forced upon changelings by the True Fae. Then, we discuss Seemings, which are the methods of escape manifested. This all occurs for your changeling character before play starts. <br /> <br /> Chapter Two: The Roles We Play Then, we give a primer on where we are now. This is a high-concept overview of Changeling: The Lost\u2019s most important game concepts. New players should be able to understand and dive in just understanding this introductory material. <br /> <br /> Chapter Three: The Laws We Live By These are the rules for changeling characters. This tells you how to actually make your changeling characters, as well as the mystical abilities they wield. If you\u2019re already familiar with the Chronicles of Darkness core rules, this section will build upon that knowledge. <br /> <br /> Chapter Four: The Tools We Wield This chapter is a truncated, Changeling-specific version of the Chronicles of Darkness core rules. This allows you to play with this book alone, without referencing other texts. <br /> <br /> Chapter Five: The Things We Fear Here, we discuss the fae monsters and other threats to changeling existence. This includes a primer on the Hedge, the gateway between the flesh world and Arcadia. <br /> <br /> Chapter Six: The Company We Keep Here, we show you how to build your own freeholds and Courts for play, as well as providing a handful of sample freeholds from all over the world as plug-and-play examples. <br /> <br /> Chapter Seven: The Stories We Tell This is material to help tell stronger stories, and frame the book\u2019s content. This gives tricks and tips for building a better game, and hitting on the strengths of Changeling: The Lost in poignant ways. <br /> <br /> Appendix One: Babes in the Woods This chapter offers a supplementary or alternative mode of play, in the form of humans touched by fae magic, who show subtle signs of the strange. These characters can add depth to your stories, or offer a different way of telling stories about the fae. <br /> <br /> Appendix Two: Conditions This reference chapter details the various Conditions mentioned throughout the book, for ease of access in play. &quot; <br /> <br /> From the introduction.<br /> <br /> So we've seen Chapter 1 &amp; 3, large parts of chapter 5, 6, &amp; Appendix 1 but we haven't really seen yet Chapters 2, 4, &amp; 7. Appendix 2 will most likely be filled mostly with what <br /> we expect will be in there.<br /> <br /> The First supplement The Hedge, obviously have more detail on the Hedge, hence the name. But its been suggested that it will include a new Seeming, several new courts/freeholds (with the court contracts that go with them), and talk about how freeholds effect the local Hedge. I'd be shocked if there wasn't new Tokens and Goblin fruits/Oddments.<br /> <br /> So ask yourself what else should go into the Hedge Supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:27:00-07:00","id":992528,"title":"","content":"I don't think we've even seem all of chapter three. It doesn't include all of the contacts. We haven't seen Tailspinning or Emotion contracts yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:31:23-07:00","id":992531,"title":"","content":"The Touchstone merit is also missing from chapter three. We've house-ruled it to function the same as the vampire merit, but I think it'll be at least somewhat mechanically different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:44:22-07:00","id":992651,"title":"","content":"I think its mostly simular, touchstones are grant willpower almost like an extra vice/virtue, and add dice to rolls to maintain humanity/clarity, the only difference I think is that Touchstones for Vampires are +2 for one touchstone, and +3 for multiple touchstones, were as for Changelings they add +1 die per dot of the touchstone merit and I don't think Changelings have to tie their Touchstones to Clarity the way Vampires do to Humanity.<br /> <br /> So yeah a slight difference in mechanics, but basically the same purpose, keep them grounded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:47:04-07:00","id":992653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=992528#post992528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we've even seem all of chapter three. It doesn't include all of the contacts. We haven't seen Tailspinning or Emotion contracts yet.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think court contracts are in the Court Chapter, we have seen a couple court contracts for the Honsu courts.<br /> <br /> But we haven't seen the goblin contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T04:06:36-07:00","id":992878,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure Goblin Contracts aren't a thing anymore. Or, rather, all Contracts work like the old goblin ones now. All you need is a Ban, which some of Contracts have. And the prominance of Goblin Vows kind of makes the entire idea of Goblin Contracts meaningless - more flexible and just as cheap.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I seem to recall an old Goblin Contract that pushed an opponent away from you when activated, I don't remember seeing that. There is also the Contracts of Sacrifice and Blood Binding which aren't closely reproduced. Well, Contract of Abjuration is better than blood binding, So I wouldn't worry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T04:37:55-07:00","id":992886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=992878#post992878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure Goblin Contracts aren't a thing anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chapter 3 Draft that was recently previewed talks about Goblin Contracts still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T04:59:56-07:00","id":992891,"title":"","content":"Which means exactly nothing. There are still references to changelings having Virtue and Vice, but listing Meins and Masks. Become the Primal Foundation is mentioned in the merit section, but there is no such thing. Rather, we have the Elemental clause of the Contract of Phantom Glory. Outdated references still exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T05:09:30-07:00","id":992892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=992891#post992891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which means exactly nothing. There are still references to changelings having Virtue and Vice, but listing Meins and Masks. Become the Primal Foundation is mentioned in the merit section, but there is no such thing. Rather, we have the Elemental clause of the Contract of Phantom Glory. Outdated references still exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more suggesting there is no evidence that they have been removed. They could simply be in a different section of the book such as a section on the goblin markets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T05:39:57-07:00","id":992897,"title":"","content":"I'm going by comments from writers. Take that as you will. Maybe what I heard is outdated, but that is what I'm going with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-25-2016, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:46:35-07:00","id":993145,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure Goblin Contracts still exist. Sean did mention that they work more or less like regular Contracts but they require a payment of blood, tears, and/or spit. And in fact, or was in response to someone asking if Goblin Vow was replacing Goblin Contracts. An argument then ensued regarding whether the terminology was significantly confusing as to merit a name change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-25-2016, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:47:30-07:00","id":993226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=993145#post993145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure Goblin Contracts still exist. Sean did mention that they work more or less like regular Contracts but they require a payment of blood, tears, and/or spit. And in fact, or was in response to someone asking if Goblin Vow was replacing Goblin Contracts. An argument then ensued regarding whether the terminology was significantly confusing as to merit a name change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus two other things.<br /> <br /> Mind you, that was a while ago. I dunno what the plans are currently for Goblin Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:30:23-07:00","id":993278,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if they were delayed to The Hedge, especially with how full the Core book seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:16:32-07:00","id":993439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=993278#post993278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be surprised if they were delayed to The Hedge, especially with how full the Core book seems.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's possible, but I'd be surprised of we didn't get at least one or two examples of Goblin contracts.<br /> <br /> We do know that both universal contracts and goblin contracts use Wyrd in their dice pools, but Court Contracts use Mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:53:58-07:00","id":993717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=992428#post992428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First supplement The Hedge, obviously have more detail on the Hedge, hence the name. But its been suggested that it will include a new Seeming, several new courts/freeholds (with the court contracts that go with them), and talk about how freeholds effect the local Hedge. I'd be shocked if there wasn't new Tokens and Goblin fruits/Oddments.<br /> <br /> So ask yourself what else should go into the Hedge Supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, also, Dark Eras also has an additional seeming for its Changeling 2E chapter, the Grimms. They escaped the Hedge by promising it they'd assume a narrative role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:23:44-07:00","id":993768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/987080-what-s-been-left-out-of-2nd-edition?p=993717#post993717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, also, Dark Eras also has an additional seeming for its Changeling 2E chapter, the Grimms. They escaped the Hedge by promising it they'd assume a narrative role.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, but its not usable in 2e without house ruling, well written chapter, but that was my biggest disappointment. No ones fault, just a victim of timing.<br /> <br /> Honestly I hope David can find room in The Hedge for an updated verison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}